cloud-appstores-how-title = How It Works
cloud-appstores-step-1 = <strong>Purchase</strong> the package for your desired store(s). We'll create an invoice and send you the onboarding questionnaire.
cloud-appstores-step-2 = <strong>Prepare credentials.</strong> We guide you through creating the necessary accounts (Google Service Account / Apple Developer) and collecting the API keys.
cloud-appstores-step-3 = <strong>We handle the submission.</strong> Our team prepares your store listing, uploads the build, and submits for review. We handle rejections and resubmissions.
cloud-appstores-step-4 = <strong>You're live!</strong> Once approved, your app is published. You retain full ownership of the developer account and all published assets.
cloud-appstores-faq-title = Frequently Asked Questions
cloud-appstores-faq-1-q = What do I need to provide?
cloud-appstores-faq-1-a = Your app binary (.aab for Android, .ipa for iOS), app icon, screenshots, description, and any necessary API credentials. We guide you through each step.
cloud-appstores-faq-2-q = How long does the process take?
cloud-appstores-faq-2-a = Google Play review typically takes 1–3 days. Apple App Store review takes 1–7 days. Account creation takes 24–48 hours for Apple, instant for Google.
cloud-appstores-faq-3-q = What if my app gets rejected?
cloud-appstores-faq-3-a = We handle resubmissions at no additional cost. Our team ensures your app meets all store guidelines before the first submission.
cloud-appstores-faq-4-q = Do I keep ownership of the developer account?
cloud-appstores-faq-4-a = Yes! The developer account is created in your name with your credentials. We only assist in the setup and submission process.
cloud-appstores-faq-5-q = Can I publish without a developer account yet?
cloud-appstores-faq-5-a = Absolutely. We include the account setup consultation in the package. For Google Play ($25 one-time) and Apple ($99/year), the store fees are separate.
